description:
Clark Wilson LLP is Hiring an Office Services Assistant

  Who We Are

  Clark Wilson LLP is a leading, innovative law firm in British Columbia. For over 100 years, we’ve proudly advised clients on a comprehensive range of legal issues and with over 200 professionals serving some of the most recognizable brands in the world, we’ve built a culture of collaboration, inclusivity, and excellence.

  As leaders in our markets, we continue to grow by fostering strong relationships, delivering exceptional service, and empowering our people to succeed. We are consistently recognized for our professional achievements, and we take pride in creating a workplace where people enjoy coming to work every day.

  How You’ll Help Us Better Service Our Clients

  We are seeking an Office Services Assistant to join our Office Services team. This is a full-time, permanent position— ideal for individuals who are eager for growth, committed to excellence, and looking to build their career in a collaborative environment.

  What You’ll Be Doing

  You are detail-oriented, proactive, and thrive in a team environment. You enjoy contributing to high-quality work while providing outstanding support to clients and colleagues.

  Daily responsibilities and tasks include, but are not limited to:

  Office Services


  Daily mail sorting and delivery;
  Coordinating courier services;
  High-volume photocopying and print support for legal professionals;
  Responding to staff and lawyer requests, including office supplies and furniture moves;
  Managing and replenishing copy room supplies, including lifting and moving boxes of paper (up to 25 lbs).


  Host Services


  Maintaining shared kitchen and break areas on a daily schedule;
  Loading and unloading firm dishwashers while remaining available for time-sensitive clients and meeting needs;
  Coordinating service and maintenance for kitchen appliances and coffee equipment;
  Stocking and maintaining boardrooms, break areas, and kitchens with appropriate dishware and supplies;
  Supporting meetings and events, including room setup, hot beverage service, catered food coordination, and schedule oversight to ensure meetings run smoothly;
  Liaising with external vendors and catering partners.


  Reception


  Providing reception coverage as required.


  How You’ll Be a Great Fit for This Role

  We’re looking for someone who brings both skills and mindset:


  Prior customer service experience;
  Experience in a professional services environment;
  Excellent verbal and written communication skills;
  Flexible and adaptable;
  Strong aptitude for technology and comfortable working with MS Office, Windows, and PCs;
  Ability to provide outstanding customer service to a variety of internal clients;
  The ability to handle stringent deadlines and work with a large volume of tasks, with interruptions and changing priorities;
  Excellent organizational skills, with exceptional attention to detail;
  The ability to exercise sound judgment, discretion, confidentiality, and adapt to changing demands;
  Ability to build rapport with the team, and provide timely support; and
  The ability to work both independently and as part of a large collegial team


  The Exciting Extras

  In addition to a competitive salary of $48,000 – $54,000, we provide a comprehensive benefits package to help you thrive at work and at home:


  Health Coverage: Medical, dental, vision, prescriptions, paramedical services, life insurance, and overseas emergency medical care.
  Retirement Planning: RRSP matching program.
  Pregnancy & Parental Leave: Top-up benefits to 100% of salary for a portion of your leave.
  Health & Wellness Spending Account: Flexible coverage for what matters most to you—whether that’s fitness classes, an exercise bike, or your pet’s vet bills.
  Recognition: Long service bonuses and celebrations.
  Work-Life Balance: Generous vacation, bonus days, five personal days, plus a paid day off on your work anniversary.
  Community & Culture: Weekly socials, team-building events, employee appreciation week, and opportunities to give back through firm-led initiatives.
  Professional Growth: Training and resources to support your personal and career development.
  Referral Program: Generous bonuses for successful employee referrals.


  How to Apply

  Click the blue “Apply” button to submit your application.

  Clark Wilson LLP is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. Diversity, inclusion, and respect are fundamental to our culture—we don’t just celebrate them, we rely on them to drive innovation, foster belonging, and grow together.

  To learn more about what it’s like to work at Clark Wilson, visit our Careers Page: www.cwilson.com

  We thank all applicants for their interest. Only those selected for an interview will be contacted.
